  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math> reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sr</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math> to yield an ionic salt.&nbsp;Choose the incorrect option related to this reaction from the following</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fbByC",
      "text": "<p>Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sr</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math> elements are present in the ionic salt</p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iiUfw",
      "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math>is tetrahedrally coordinated in the ionic salt</p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "H59H7",
      "text": "<p>The element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math> is present in the cationic part of the ionic salt</p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "3Qi16",
      "text": "<p>The reaction is an example of acid-base neutralization reaction</p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;amphoteric nature.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sr</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has basic nature. These two compounds undergo acid-base reaction to get salt,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>Sr</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mi>Sr</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Be</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math> is present in anionic part.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
